  "content": "[Intro]\n[Gm]I lost myself on a\ncool damp night\n[Eb]I gave myself in that misty light\n[D7]Was hypnotized by a strange delight\nUn der a lilac tree\n[Gm]I made a wine from the\nlilac tree\n[Eb]Put my heart in its recipe\n[D7]Makes me see what I want to see\nBe what I want to be\n[Gm]\n[Fdim7]When I think more [C]than I want to think\n[D7]Do things I never should [Gm]do\n[Fdim7]I drink much more that I [C]ought to drink Because\n[Cm]it brings me back you\n[Dsus4]  [D7]\n\n[Verse 1]\n[G]\n[G7]\n[G]Lilac wine\n[G7]\n[C]is sweet and\n[D7]heady,\n[G]like my love\n[G7]\n[C]Lilac wine,\n[Dm]  [G]\n[C]I feel un-\n[Dm]steady, [G]like\n[C]my love\n\n[Chorus]\n[Eb]Listen to me, I cannot see\n[D7]clearly Isn't that she,\ncoming to me near-\n[Am]ly here?\n[D7]\n\n[Verse 2]\n[G]Lilac\n[G7]wine\n[C]is sweet and\n[D7]heady where's\n[G]my love?\n[G7]\n[C]Lilac wine,\n[Dm]  [G]\n[C]I feel un-\n[Dm]steady, [G]where's\n[C]my love?\n\n[Chorus]\n[Eb]Listen to me, why is everything so\n[D7]hazy? Isn't that she,\nor am I just going cra-\n[Am]zy, dear?\n[D7]\n\n[Outro]\n[G]Lilac\n[G7]wine,\n[C]I feel un-\n[D7]ready for\n[G]my love\n[G7]Feel\n[C]unready\n[Am7-5][D7]for\nmy love\n[G]",
